  "text": "At the usual time, Mara will still be working. We can start later, or you can read the story she sent.\n\nThe large lump did not bake evenly. Rina sets it aside. Make a new batch with the remaining dry flour.\n\nA notebook for moments you took part in. Add your own thoughts or arrange the cards whenever you like.\n\nArrange pictures of moments you took part in. Any order is welcome; this never changes what happened.\n\nAn earlier boat arrival · You guide Mara. The boy holds the bird his sister made for his grandmother.\n\nGrandma has heard Sol’s story. She wants to understand why he stopped bringing stories before today.\n\nThe deck reaches both banks, but an end is loose. Pip can try it, or you can fasten both ends first.\n\nThese cards remember completed actions and tellings. Related pages open with the usual reading help.\n\nSuggested picture: Rina thanks Sol. Your current picture stays selected until you choose this one.\n\nMara says: “Please do. If I’m still at work, I’d love to read one of Grandma’s stories afterward.”\n\nRina carries the thank-you loaf. She is waiting for Pip or walking with him along the bakery path.\n\nThe last passenger boat is returning. Mara will help everyone ashore before joining the gathering.\n\nGrandma has shared her story. Choose the moment to keep in Pip’s flower during your conversation.\n\nThe whole telling plays automatically. Pause, replay or open the complete text with reading help.\n\nThat’s two minutes. Your microphone is off. You can review this reading or record a shorter part.\n\nPip is carrying the seed in his backpack. Prepare the spot, place the seed and cover it together.\n\nOpenAI feedback is available for this activity in this local demo. Hints are prepared story help.",
